class:: Oscnet
summary:: Coupled-oscillator network with nonlinear feedback
related:: Classes/Limcycle, Classes/Diststoch
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic

description::

A network of detuned organ-style oscillators that modulate each other's pitch, sum
through a shapeable nonlinearity, and feed a fraction of that result back into the whole
bank. It takes the "organismic", non-hierarchical idea of SOMA's Lyra-8 and exposes the
network itself:

list::
## code::voices:: sets the number of oscillators, 1–64 (fixed at build time).
## code::topo:: selects the coupling graph: 0 pairs (0↔1, 2↔3…), 1 ring (nearest
neighbours), 2 all-to-all (mean field). The topology, not a preset, defines the organism.
## code::couple:: is the cross-modulation strength; code::feedback:: routes the
distorted sum back into every voice's pitch, so past a threshold the drone self-collapses.
## code::fold:: morphs the nonlinearity from tanh saturation (0) to triangle wavefolding (1).
## code::drift:: applies a slow stochastic random-walk to each voice's tuning (organic
instability, reusing Tether's stochastic core).
::

Two outputs: code::[shaped, clean]::. For a Lyra-style mod-delay, patch the output through
link::Classes/CombC:: / link::Classes/AllpassC:: in your SynthDef.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: freq
Centre frequency (Hz). Default 110.
argument:: voices
Oscillator count, 1–64 (fixed). Default 4.
argument:: spread
Detune ratio between voices (1 = unison). Default 1.01.
argument:: topo
Coupling graph: 0 pairs, 1 ring, 2 all-to-all. Default 0.
argument:: couple
Cross-modulation strength. Default 0.2.
argument:: modFreq
Shared vibrato (hyper-LFO) rate (Hz). Default 0.3.
argument:: modDepth
Shared vibrato depth. Default 0.05.
argument:: fold
Nonlinearity morph: 0 tanh saturation, 1 triangle wavefold. Default 0.
argument:: drive
Drive into the nonlinearity. Default 2.
argument:: feedback
Post-shaping feedback into voice pitch, 0–0.99. Default 0.2.
argument:: drift
Stochastic detune random-walk amount, 0–1. Default 0.
argument:: mul
argument:: add

examples::
code::
{ Oscnet.ar(110, 6, 1.02, MouseX.kr(0, 2).round(1), 0.6, 0.3, 0.05, 0, 2, 0.3)[0] * 0.15 ! 2 }.play;

{ Oscnet.ar(110, 4, 1.01, 0, 0.3, 0.3, 0.05, 0, 2, MouseX.kr(0, 0.95))[0] * 0.2 ! 2 }.play;

{ Oscnet.ar(110, 8, 1.01, 2, MouseX.kr(0, 1.5))[0] * 0.15 ! 2 }.play;

{ Oscnet.ar(140, 4, 1.02, 0, 0.5, 0.2, 0.05, MouseX.kr(0, 1), 3, 0.3)[0] * 0.15 ! 2 }.play;

{ Oscnet.ar(90, 6, 1.03, 1, 0.5, 0.2, 0.08, 0, 2, 0.4, MouseX.kr(0, 1))[0] * 0.15 ! 2 }.play;
::
